  "message": "interactive: keep the original input in the history with isympy -I\n\nWith isympy -I every cell was rewritten through tokenize.untokenize\nbefore being passed to run_cell. untokenize without token positions\npads every token with spaces, and because the rewritten text was handed\nto run_cell as the raw cell it was also what IPython stored in the\nhistory, so pressing the up arrow recalled e.g.\n\"eo =solveset (sin (x ),x )\" instead of what was typed.\n\nint_to_Integer now splices Integer(...) into the original source using\nthe token positions, so spacing and comments survive, and the rewrite is\nregistered as an IPython input transformer so the history keeps the\noriginal input. The run_cell wrapper is only used as a fallback for\nIPython versions without input_transformers_post.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
 },
